.TH LN 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
ln \- make links between files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ln
[\fB\-s\fR] [\fB\-f\fR] \fITARGET\fR \fILINK_NAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a link named LINK_NAME to TARGET. Hard links by default; \fB\-s\fR makes a symbolic link instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-symbolic
Make a symbolic link instead of a hard link.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Remove an existing LINK_NAME before linking.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a general failure (a listed file could not be processed, etc.), 2 on a usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
